{"event_type":"review","id":"6a038f5dadd1ebb92a3680277c157797eb9dd4ef912d8a19be18a2c38e615a0f","occurred_at":"2026-11-09T19:00:12Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b378657c79bab608ba298beaafc0453c8ecc3eda02c162b7c08d7253e8555510","sha256":"b378657c79bab608ba298beaafc0453c8ecc3eda02c162b7c08d7253e8555510"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b0d7bc3f8700515283f2f4ef4a4cd5a8cb38b26cd590e27ace71c1eeaca5f0a5","sha256":"b0d7bc3f8700515283f2f4ef4a4cd5a8cb38b26cd590e27ace71c1eeaca5f0a5"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3fb78dbe29e52a94c9cc0ff166607081f19607b8d786f5e529f100c55e7d5e1c","sha256":"3fb78dbe29e52a94c9cc0ff166607081f19607b8d786f5e529f100c55e7d5e1c"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4082a94190e24473fcf97a90379acd72d87648fb8331dba73b92115f2430062d","sha256":"4082a94190e24473fcf97a90379acd72d87648fb8331dba73b92115f2430062d"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/bc5f1f4e2c113a2f9350d02a83510a63ab482cf1b1a89a606a5b32a228919497","sha256":"bc5f1f4e2c113a2f9350d02a83510a63ab482cf1b1a89a606a5b32a228919497"}],"attempt_id":"6baee7d88ada1f7546380f6c0830676b29466463498d48c7d41dd39b7a82e306:0:1","base":"d2efe0702219bbe05fa2cd7c8dc6fcffc3384069","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"e6b0bb420e93d21e34c51f13e4de96de31d8f34b","body":"**Counts can be double-booked: `counts[category]` is incremented before the code that can still raise.**\n\nLine 114 increments the category count. Lines 115-119 then read `capture[\"target\"]`, call `targets.add(...)`, and call `path.get(...)`. These lines can raise `KeyError`, `TypeError`, or `AttributeError`. Examples are an unhashable `target` or a non-dict `paths` entry. The `except` at Line 120 then increments `unverified` for the same item. The item is counted as `proven_terminal`, `partial_scope`, or another category and also as `unverified`. The totals then exceed the number of receipts. This also reports a receipt that failed validation as proven.\n\nCollect `target` and `exclusions` into locals first. Commit them and the category count only after the whole `try` body succeeds.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-            counts[category] += 1\n-            targets.add(capture[\"target\"])\n-            for path in capture[\"paths\"]:\n-                disposition = path.get(\"disposition\", \"unknown\")\n-                if disposition not in (\"included\", \"renamed\"):\n-                    exclusions[disposition] = exclusions.get(disposition, 0) + 1\n+            target = capture[\"target\"]\n+            hash(target)\n+            skipped = [path.get(\"disposition\", \"unknown\") for path in capture[\"paths\"]]\n+            counts[category] += 1\n+            targets.add(target)\n+            for disposition in skipped:\n+                if disposition not in (\"included\", \"renamed\"):\n+                    exclusions[disposition] = exclusions.get(disposition, 0) + 1\n```\n</details>","id":"71140745252128b2af38c98036c30c50d11ccb0fe733bc8d521b4cbea74a7ea6","intervals":[[114,119]],"path":"apps/crq-python/status_summary.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Counts can be double-booked: `counts[category]` is incremented before the code that can still raise."}],"head":"5c8c6d26af343e967f92c8d800b99cf7ab9e476b","head_tree":"59a8e4bccb16679adcf515ad27331e6995a154f0","input_scope":[{"blob":"7126e4260de4df8e05634b228e73d5cc62b139c5","intervals":[[5,12],[18,58],[61,62],[64,116],[120,122],[126,130],[146,162],[165,165],[167,168],[171,182],[186,188],[193,195],[198,242],[248,256],[260,260],[264,264],[291,294]],"path":"apps/crq-python/README.md"},{"blob":"e6b0bb420e93d21e34c51f13e4de96de31d8f34b","intervals":[[3,3],[5,7],[9,9],[